  "_schema": {
    "wire": "live = the seat posts its own status automatically (API/agent access). reported = a human or scheduled job relays its Report Block. The office shows this per desk so you always know how much to trust a screen.",
    "status": "working | shipped | yellow | red | idle | nosignal",
    "idle_vs_nosignal": "idle means the seat has nothing assigned and honestly has nothing to do — drawn feet-up. nosignal means we have not heard from it inside run.staleAfterMinutes — drawn as an empty chair with a dark screen. Never collapse these two; an office that renders silence as rest is lying to you.",
    "place": "room = this task is shared or cross-lane, so the seat is drawn in the war room. desk = own-lane work. Set from the PLACE field of the seat's Report Block.",
    "artifact": "{ name, url } — what is literally on the seat's screen right now. Set from the ARTIFACT field of the Report Block.",
    "phase2": "Serve this from GET /board on the Worker and accept POST /board/:seat for live-wired seats. See ops/02-MEETING-PROTOCOL.md."
